    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 81.21 efficiency score. Facing Rocker, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong SP skill advantage and a favorable leadoff spot, making him our primary offensive engine. Joining him at the top of the projected performance tier are **Andy Pages** (74.43), **Jackson Merrill** (74.20), and **Kyle Tucker** (75.28). **Andy Pages** is a particularly intriguing play; while his raw base is lower than **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s, he draws a positive variance bump from Rodriguez\u2019s slow delivery, which historically opens up stolen base opportunities\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on speed. **Jackson Merrill**, while currently pending official lineup confirmation, remains an essential start due to a significant SP skill advantage against Javier, even with a slight negative park adjustment.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Nasim Nunez** (58.06) in the UTIL spot over **Coby Mayo** (45.68). While **Coby Mayo** offers superior power potential, his score was dragged down by a negative platoon differential against Rocker and a bottom-tier batting order assignment. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** provides essential, scarce speed and solid efficiency, justifying the final starting spot. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Heliot Ramos** (62.98); while he projects well against Holmes, his score is slightly suppressed by the catcher\u2019s elite pop time, which limits his stolen base ceiling. **Drake Baldwin** faces the toughest test of the day against Schlittler; his sub-50 score is a direct result of a negative SP skill adjustment, marking him as a high-risk play for today\u2019s production.\n\nRisk management remains paramount, specifically with **Jackson Merrill** awaiting a finalized batting order. We are comfortable with his placement in the #5 hole based on current intel, but any shift lower in the lineup would require a reassessment of his efficiency score. Additionally, we are monitoring the BvP weakness for **Kyle Tucker** against Rodriguez; while the projection favors the talent of **Kyle Tucker** regardless of the 27-PA sample size, it serves as a reminder that we are prioritizing overall process over extreme micro-situational splits. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the bench, as his projection (41.74) simply cannot overcome the harsh negative platoon dynamic and elite-level catchers he is scheduled to face today.",
